hadiths[11]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1575","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: O Banu Abd al-Muttalib (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) O Banu Abd Manaf, do not stop anyone who is performing Tawaf of this House of Allah (or near it), because the morning prayer is not a prayer until the sun rises, and after the Asr prayer, there is no prayer until the sun sets. However, the order near this house in Mecca is different. (Here) people can circumambulate (at these times) and pray."
"1576",": Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, it is obligatory for him to perform the Friday prayer on Friday. He will take care of this person, and Allah is Careless and Praiseworthy."
"1577","-: Tariq bin Shahab narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him: It is obligatory for all people to read Fridays, not only for the four: a slave, a (minor) child, a sick person and a woman."
"1578",": Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: (We are the ones who will come later and the Day of Resurrection will be the ones ahead). The reason for this is: Those people were given the Book before us and we were given the Book after them. So this is the Day that Allah made obligatory on these people and then Allah guided us about it, so people are our followers in this regard. The Jewish day is tomorrow (Saturday) and the Christian day is the day after (Saturday)."
"1579","-: Ata bin Abi Rabah narrates this saying of Sayyiduna Jabar bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu: This method is being used: When three people are present, one of them will be the imam, and where there are forty people or more, there will be Friday prayer, Eid al-Zuha prayer, and Eid al-Fitr prayer. The reason for this is: these people are considered as one congregation."
"1580","- Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: (in a village) there are fifty people, Jumu'ah will be obligatory on them, and it will not be obligatory on less than that."
"1581",": 1563 Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said this: It is obligatory to pray Jumu'ah for fifty people."
"1582",": 1564 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): It is not necessary for a traveler to read Friday."
"1583",": 1565 Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: A certain Prophet (PBUH) was giving a sermon to us on Friday. At the same time, a caravan came with grain and that caravan stopped in an open field. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) revealed this verse: And when they saw the thing of trade and interest, they went towards it and left you in a state of stay."
"1584",": 1566 Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was giving a sermon while standing on Friday. Meanwhile, a caravan came (After that, the narrator has narrated the entire hadith, after which these words follow):"
"1585","Muhammad bin Abu Umamah narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b (may God be pleased with him) regarding his father: I used to take my father with me when his sight was gone. Once I took him to perform the Friday prayer. After hearing the call to prayer, he prayed for mercy and asked for forgiveness for Sayyiduna Abu Umamah. asked them: O Abajan! Every time you hear the call to prayer on Friday, you pray for forgiveness for Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu. What is the reason for this? So he replied: O my son! He (Sayyidna Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him) was the first person who started Jumu'ah in the low ground of the stone yellow plain of Banu Bayadah in Madinah, the name of this place is \Naqi' al-Khuzmat\"". So they replied: There were forty persons."""
